# U4 harness object bytes, measured on the local Linux host's persistent
# harness object directory for reviewed test262 shard 1/10 at total 10.
# Directory:
#   $XDG_CACHE_HOME/oseo/harness-objects
# pointed at the U4 session scratchpad, so the numbers cover that shard's
# objects only. Both entries are verbatim command and output from the U4
# session; the timestamps are that tool call's own, converted to +09:00.
# Objects are linux-x86_64-gnu; no macOS object bytes were measured.

== 2026-09-27T21:20:14+09:00  superseded, taken mid-run at 92 objects
$ D="$XDG_CACHE_HOME/oseo/harness-objects"; cd "$D" \
    && tar -cf - *.o 2>/dev/null | zstd -3 -T0 -c 2>/dev/null | wc -c \
    | awk '{print "zstd3 bytes:", $1, "MB:", $1/1048576}'; \
  find . -name '*.o' -printf '%s\n' \
    | awk '{s+=$1} END {print "raw MB:", s/1048576, "n:", NR}'
zstd3 bytes: 35083833 MB: 33.4586
raw MB: 226.045 n: 92

# The first cold run was still building when this ran, so it covers 92 of the
# shard's 96 objects. The 33.5 MB and 226.0 MB values it produced are not the
# ones the baseline cites; the complete measurement below replaced them.

== 2026-09-28T01:31:58+09:00  complete, all 96 objects of the shard
$ D="$XDG_CACHE_HOME/oseo/harness-objects"; \
  find "$D" -name '*.o' -printf '%s\n' | sort -n \
    | awk '{a[NR]=$1; s+=$1} END {printf "n=%d total=%d totalMB=%.1f meanMB=%.2f minMB=%.2f maxMB=%.2f\n", NR, s, s/1048576, s/NR/1048576, a[1]/1048576, a[NR]/1048576}'; \
  cd "$D" && tar -cf - *.o | zstd -3 -T0 -c | wc -c \
    | awk '{printf "zstd3 bytes=%d MB=%.1f\n", $1, $1/1048576}'
n=96 total=251067584 totalMB=239.4 meanMB=2.49 minMB=0.60 maxMB=6.47
zstd3 bytes=37173060 MB=35.5

# The MB columns are the awk divisions by 1048576 above, so they are binary
# megabytes; the exact byte totals are 251067584 and 37173060. The compression
# invocation is the whole `tar -cf - *.o | zstd -3 -T0 -c` pipeline, with zstd
# level 3 and all threads, counted by `wc -c` rather than written to a file.
